### Defining the benefits of the AWS Cloud 

#### what is cloud computing in terms of AWS?

    1 - On-demand Self-service - which is the ability to provision compute capabilities, on demand when that service is needed. Cloud computing also has to provision resources without any human interaction and or intervention, to make it an On-demand self service. This can be done via the console, the command line & also through application programming interfaces. 

    2 - Access to the network - AWS gives us the ability to build, using the aws management console, Command line, http, https, vpn & more.

    3 - Resource pooling - what is resource pooling? aws provides pooled resouces to serve multiple aws customers. AWS has thousands of servers, databases & morew, that we can on-demand provision & build in our own environment.

    4 - elasticity - Elasticity is the ability to scale with demand. As your demand increases, elasticity can scale up your resources, when your demand decreases, elasticity can scale it down to meet your businesses needs.

    5 - Resource usage monitored and billed - with AWS, you are no longer pre-provisioning and or procuring your storage, your compute etc. you no longer have to estimate your demands, because AWS they have services that are monitored for usage & then billed, but aws scales your resources to meet your demand, instead of being over or under provisioned. The biggest cost benefit is that you only pay for what you use within AWS.
        
